tannu.etymology:
Uncertain; proposals include:
# from Vulgar Latin *tandō;
# from Latin tandem;
# from a merger of the two above (if so, it also applies to the other descendants of *tandō);
# from Latin ante annum;
# from a contraption of tali annu.

anciḍḍa.etymology:
From the palatalization of Latin anguilla,
from an earlier Proto-Italic *anɣʷis,
from Proto-Indo-European *h₂éngʷʰis (“water-worm, eel”). Compare Friulian anzile, Sardinian anguidda, Catalan and Spanish anguila.
